4. TIGERGRAPH — GRAPH-BASED RETRIEVAL FOR SEARCH & RECOMMENDATION

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

4.1 Why Graph + Vector Search?

  Vector search captures SEMANTIC SIMILARITY:
    "cheap eats" → "budget restaurants" (embeddings are close)
    
  Graph traversal captures STRUCTURAL RELATIONSHIPS:
    "the restaurant John mentioned" → User→John→Conversations→Restaurants
    "fraud rings" → Card→Device→OtherCards (shared attributes)

  Neither alone is sufficient. Combined = hybrid retrieval.

4.2 TigerGraph Architecture

  Component          Description
  Storage            Distributed graph, partitioned by vertex type
  Query Language     GSQL — SQL-like with graph traversal primitives  
  Traversal          Multi-hop with filters, aggregations, accumulators
  Throughput         Millions of vertices/sec per node
  Real-Time          Sub-second for 2-3 hop on billion-edge graphs
  REST API           Every query auto-exposes as REST endpoint

4.3 Graph Schema for Search & Recommendation

  // Fraud Detection Graph
  CREATE VERTEX Card (PRIMARY_ID id STRING, bin STRING, issuer STRING)
  CREATE VERTEX Merchant (PRIMARY_ID id STRING, mcc STRING, name STRING)
  CREATE VERTEX Device (PRIMARY_ID id STRING, fingerprint STRING)
  CREATE VERTEX IP (PRIMARY_ID id STRING, geo STRING)
  
  CREATE DIRECTED EDGE Transaction (FROM Card, TO Merchant,
      amount DOUBLE, timestamp UINT, channel STRING)
  CREATE UNDIRECTED EDGE SharedDevice (FROM Card, TO Device)
  CREATE UNDIRECTED EDGE SharedIP (FROM Card, TO IP)

  // Siri Knowledge Graph
  CREATE VERTEX User (PRIMARY_ID id STRING, name STRING)
  CREATE VERTEX Contact (PRIMARY_ID id STRING, name STRING,
      name_embedding LIST<DOUBLE>, phone STRING)
  CREATE VERTEX Place (PRIMARY_ID id STRING, name STRING,
      embedding LIST<DOUBLE>, category STRING)
  CREATE VERTEX App (PRIMARY_ID id STRING, name STRING)
  
  CREATE DIRECTED EDGE Knows (FROM User, TO Contact, frequency UINT)
  CREATE DIRECTED EDGE VisitedPlace (FROM User, TO Place, timestamp UINT)
  CREATE DIRECTED EDGE UsesApp (FROM User, TO App, frequency UINT)
  CREATE DIRECTED EDGE MentionedIn (FROM Contact, TO Place, timestamp UINT)

4.4 Hybrid Retrieval Pattern

  Step 1: Graph retrieval (TigerGraph)
    → 2-3 hop traversal from user/entity
    → Returns candidate set with graph-based scores
    → Features: degree centrality, component size, edge weights

  Step 2: Vector retrieval (FAISS on GPU)
    → kNN search against embedding index
    → Returns candidate set with similarity scores

  Step 3: Fusion
    → Merge candidates, combine scores (learned weights)
    → Deduplicate on entity ID

  Step 4: Re-rank
    → Cross-encoder or gradient-boosted model
    → Sees both graph features + embedding distances

  Step 5: Serve
    → Top-K results → downstream consumer

